    "body": "Problem:\nHandlers keep one pending BufRead autocmd per namespace to show\ndiagnostics on an unloaded buffer. Showing or hiding diagnostics on any\nother buffer in the namespace deletes it, so the unloaded buffer shows\nnothing once loaded. If that buffer was wiped, the delete fails with\n\"Failed to delete autocmd\", and so does every later show() or hide() in\nthe namespace.\n\nIntroduced by a1bc5d0ae6, which keeps only the latest pending autocmd\nto avoid showing stale diagnostics.\n\nSolution:\nKeep the latest pending show per buffer, handler and namespace, and run\nthem from one global BufRead autocmd, like #40869 does for positions.\n\nAI-assisted\n",
    "closed_at": null,
